  <heading>SLBND</heading>
  <desc>
    <brief>
      <para>Scoped release boundary</para>
    </brief>
    <authored>
      <para>This instruction signals to the memory system that a corresponding instruction with Release semantics
or <instruction>DMB</instruction> instruction will subsequently occur in program order, and if that
corresponding instruction defines a Barrier scope with the <instruction>SLBND</instruction> instruction,
then these instructions do not create a Barrier-ordered-before relationship between any Effect in program
order before the <instruction>SLBND</instruction> instruction and any of the following:</para>
      <list type="unordered">
        <listitem>
          <content>The Effect with Release semantics.</content>
        </listitem>
        <listitem>
          <content>Any Effect in program order after the DMB Effect.</content>
        </listitem>
      </list>
    </authored>
  </desc>
